{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Recipe",
  "recipeCuisine": "Japan",
  "name": "Chicken Karaage",
  "text": "Chicken Karaage\n\nPreparation time:\n\nCooking time:\n\nYield: 2\n\nIngredients\n\n300g boneless chicken thigh (with skin),\n\n½ tsp soy sauce,\n\n½ tbsp sake,\n\n¼ tsp salt,\n\npepper,\n\n1 tsp grated root ginger,\n\n1 tsp grated garlic,\n\n½ tsp sesame oil,\n\n½ beaten egg,\n\n2½ tbsp potato starch (or corn flour),\n\nlettuce leaves,\n\nparsley leaves,\n\nvegetable oil for deep frying.\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Prick the skin side of the chicken thigh using the tip of a knife. Turn over and trim off the fat. Cut through the tougher sinews. Prick with the tip of a knife. Cut into large bite size pieces.\n\n2. Put the chicken in a bowl and add 1/2 tsp soy sauce, 1/2 tbsp sake, 1/4 tsp salt, 1 tsp grated ginger, 1 tsp grated garlic, 1/2 tsp sesame oil, and a little pepper. Mix well, then put in the fridge for 30 minutes.\n\n3. Add the beaten egg to the chicken a little at a time, mixing with your fingers.\n\n4. Add the potato starch and lightly mix until the chicken is coated with the flour.\n\n5. Put the chicken in the pan of oil at a relatively low temperature (160C).\n\n6. Wait until the batter is firm before turning.\n\n7. When the pieces are lightly brown remove onto a draining rack.\n\n8. Heat the oil to high (180C).\n\n10. Place the chicken back into the oil.\n\n11. Remove when brown and crispy.\n\n12. Serve on a plate with the lettuce and parsley.",
  "recipeYield": "2",
